{"id":"n-20261030-o2qd3h","category":"finance","display_title":"Wall Street Falls As Tech Stocks Drop","display_title_he":"וול סטריט יורדת בעקבות נפילת מניות הטכנולוגיה","short_summary":"Wall Street closed lower as major tech companies faced steep declines following disappointing earnings reports. Meanwhile, DoorDash announced a major acquisition of Instacart.","english_level":"C1","words":408,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Benches_at_Oakes_Garden_Theatre%2C_Niagara_Falls%2C_Canada.jpg/960px-Benches_at_Oakes_Garden_Theatre%2C_Niagara_Falls%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Maksim Sokolov (maxergon.com) · CC BY-SA 4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Benches_at_Oakes_Garden_Theatre,_Niagara_Falls,_Canada.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001561197","title":"וול סטריט ננעלה בירידות; אלפאבית מחקה היום כחצי טריליון דולר משוויה","published_at":"2026-10-29T20:00:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-29T20:00:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:30.325Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Wall Street experienced a notable downturn, driven primarily by weakness in the technology sector following disappointing third-quarter financial results from major corporations. According to market data, the tech-heavy Nasdaq dropped significantly, while the S&P 500 and the Dow Jones Industrial Average also finished the trading session in negative territory. Analysts noted that investors are becoming increasingly selective, demanding clearer returns on massive artificial intelligence investments rather than offering unlimited financial backing.","Alphabet, Google's parent company, suffered its worst trading day in history, with its stock plunging by approximately 13 percent. The dramatic sell-off erased roughly half a trillion dollars from the company's market capitalization. The sharp decline followed weaker-than-expected revenue and adjusted earnings per share, alongside a negative free cash flow exceeding nine billion dollars. Market observers highlighted that these results triggered a technical bearish signal known as a death cross, reflecting ongoing concerns about near-term momentum and heavy capital expenditures.","Other technology giants and industrial firms experienced varied reactions from investors. Microsoft saw its share price fluctuate after releasing its fiscal first-quarter results. Although strong growth in its Azure cloud computing business helped the company surpass analyst expectations, lower-than-anticipated capital expenditure forecasts raised concerns regarding potential delays in data center capacity expansion. Meanwhile, Microsoft joined several competitors by finalizing a 25 billion dollar bond issuance, using debt for the first time to fund its expansive artificial intelligence infrastructure. Caterpillar also declined despite beating revenue and profit estimates, as its construction division sales fell slightly short of projections.","In the broader corporate landscape, DoorDash made significant headlines by announcing the acquisition of grocery delivery platform Instacart for 17 billion dollars in a cash-and-stock deal. The transaction offers Instacart shareholders a premium valuation based on recent market prices. Additionally, pharmaceutical giant Eli Lilly posted record-breaking quarterly results driven by robust sales of its weight-loss treatment Zepbound, causing its stock price to rise notably. Norwegian Cruise Line also surged after exceeding market forecasts for the top and bottom lines.","On the macroeconomic front, the Federal Reserve decided to leave interest rates unchanged within the 3.75 to 4 percent range, pointing out that inflation continues to run high as policymakers await additional economic data. Third-quarter economic growth data showed the US economy expanding at an annualized rate of 3.4 percent, while the Personal Consumption Expenditures price index pointed to ongoing inflationary pressures. Conversely, European stock markets finished the trading day with steady gains after the European Central Bank similarly opted to keep its benchmark interest rates untouched."],"facts":[{"fact":"Wall Street closed lower, led by technology stocks, following disappointing earnings reports from Alphabet and Caterpillar.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Alphabet shares plummeted by roughly 13%, erasing about half a trillion dollars in market value.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Microsoft issued 25 billion dollars in bonds to help finance its massive investments in artificial intelligence infrastructure.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"DoorDash announced the acquisition of Instacart for 17 billion dollars in a cash-and-stock deal.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Federal Reserve kept interest rates unchanged between 3.75% and 4%, noting that inflation remains high.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"European stock exchanges closed higher after the European Central Bank left interest rates unchanged.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Wall Street","lemma":"Wall Street","pos":"noun","he":"וול סטריט","name":"true"},{"text":"experienced","lemma":"experience","pos":"verb","he":"חווה","name":false},{"text":"notable","lemma":"notable","pos":"adjective","he":"בולט","name":false},{"text":"downturn","lemma":"downturn","pos":"noun","he":"מגמת ירידה","name":false},{"text":"driven","lemma":"drive","pos":"verb","he":"מונע על ידי","name":false},{"text":"primarily","lemma":"primarily","pos":"adverb","he":"בעיקר","name":false},{"text":"weakness","lemma":"weakness","pos":"noun","he":"חולשה","name":false},{"text":"technology","lemma":"technology","pos":"noun","he":"טכנולוגיה","name":false},{"text":"sector","lemma":"sector","pos":"noun","he":"מגזר","name":false},{"text":"following","lemma":"follow","pos":"preposi